- Cael: Ah… what a strange hour to meet, acquaintance. Step forward. The world you see is only half the truth.

* [What do you mean?]
Cael: You’ve pierced the veil. Your eyes have glimpsed beyond steel… and glimpsed what you may not yet comprehend.

Cael: Children call it power. Fools call it fire. Magic is the thin skin stretched between what is and what is not… and every spell rends that skin ever so slightly.

* [Are you the court wizard?]
Cael: Was… something of the sort. I served in my time, but now I am bound to no ruler.

Cael: I was once a scholar in a faraway place: the Veilglades. Its college drew students from all corners of the world.
<> I remember every lesson, every tome, every folly… from the betrayal of Maerimond to the dark arts’ transgressions.

Cael: When I left, the island thrived. Today… it has lost its right to exist in this world.
<> The gods have yet to banish it; its waters remain cursed. Yet the Veilglades endure in memory, at least in mine.

Cael: Fear not magic. Indulge your intelligence, for that is the way of a true mage.
<> Power will follow. But heed this: every spell demands a hidden price. One day… you will understand, though I hope it is not soon.

* [Tips]
{shuffle:

- Cael: Waste not your mana carelessly. It is a vital energy, and replenishing it may cost more than you imagine—by tonics… or the dusk cap mushroom, rare though it grows in Slepbone.

- Cael: Position is everything. Too close, and even the smallest foe may shatter your incantation.

- Cael: Some spells may be charged, their power building in patience. Hold them until the moment is right.

- Cael: Lock upon your enemies. The veil favors the focused mage.

- Cael: Weaken your foe to magic first, then strike. Even the strongest armor yields to clever application of sorcery.
}


* [Rumors]
{shuffle:
- Cael: The Veilglade University sank beneath the ocean long ago. Its library, filled with secret sorceries… lost to the depths. Such knowledge, swallowed by the sea—tragic, really.

- Cael: They say a huntress still wanders the Veilglades, striving to lift its curse. Perhaps she has glimpsed a future even I cannot see.

- Cael: The orcs and the elves… some whisper they share a common ancestry. I shall speak no more on that… some truths are best left veiled.
}

* [Goodbye]
